# QA MA (audio, audio-design §4 boss cues + Pause): pauses during the
# boss cues. cafe_zauner_tour (title flow, the Normal boss win) with two
# pauses inserted, each 200 frames (START, 198 idle, START):
# 1) at 1100, 15 frames into boss_surprise (1085). The boss loop is
#    scheduled 36 frames after the chord on the game-frame clock, so
#    `song boss` starts at 1121 while paused (silent under the hold); on
#    resume (1299) the chord's last 21 frames ring over a boss loop that is
#    already 178 frames (~3 s) in instead of starting on its bar 1.
# 2) at 2615, 2 frames into the Tusch (boss_defeat at 2613). The café
#    piece is scheduled 150 frames later (Tusch + 1 s silence) and starts
#    at 2763 while paused; on resume (2814) the Tusch's last 88 frames play
#    over cafe_zauner, which is 51 frames in: no 1 s of silence, the Tusch
#    and the café piece at once.
# Expected cue log: scheduled songs wait for the pause (start 36 / 150
# play frames after their jingle, i.e. after the resume). The replay
# passes; accept its cue golden only after the fix.
